@startuml HostInference
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how a local model reaches an sbx agent — the host's Ollama on the host GPU, one port across the VM boundary
' covers: internal/sbx/host_ollama.go (LocalModelEnv, EnsureHostOllama, HostOllamaPolicyHost)
' covers: internal/sbx/host_ollama_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/host_memory.go (memoryFor, amdFreeVRAM, parseNvidiaFree)
' covers: internal/sbx/host_memory_test.go
' covers: internal/run/local_model_fit.go (admitOversizedModel)
' covers: internal/run/local_model_fit_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/oversized_model.go (ConfirmOversizedModel)
' covers: internal/choiceui/oversized_model_test.go
' covers: internal/run/model_row.go (localModels, tagFor)
' covers: internal/run/run.go (promptChoices, launchSandbox)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Spec allow, proxyOnlyVar)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/host_inference_test.go
'   the measurements and rejected options ... _spec/_experiments/sbx-host-inference.puml
'   the model row ............................ _spec/defs/hermes/hermes-paradigm.puml
'
' ── RULE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' On sbx, ANY local model — `--local-model X` or a model-row choice — is served by
' the operator's own Ollama on the host, never inside the VM and never by a server
' proveo starts. The microVM has no GPU on macOS and a passthrough-only GPU on Linux.
' proveo checks, pulls a missing tag, and routes; it never installs, starts or
' tunes Ollama (2026-09-27: pulling added — refusing with `ollama pull` only
' made the operator retype what proveo already knew).
'
' ── SEQUENCE (launchSandbox, before the sandbox exists) ─────────────────────
' (selectBackend's sbx branch until 2026-10-16; sbx is now the only backend.)
'   1. GET 127.0.0.1:11434/api/tags. No answer ⇒ refuse with the install URL.
'   2. Tag lookup: exact, or bare name ⇒ ":latest" (Ollama's rule). Missing ⇒
'      size from registry.ollama.ai/v2/<repo>/manifests/<tag> (config + layers;
'      muse-glimmer:30b-mlx = 17.75 GiB), a WARNING if it would not fit in memory
'      right now (memory is transient, the download is not), then POST /api/pull
'      with progress on stderr. PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL_PULL=0 restores the refusal
'      (`ollama pull <tag>` + installed tags of the same repo). A non-library ref
'      (hf.co/…) pulls with no size shown.
'   3. Already in /api/ps ⇒ resident, no new memory, done.
'   4. Fit: need = size + size/8 + 1 GiB against the free memory of the POOL
'      Ollama loads into (FIT POOL below). need > free ⇒ *sbx.NoFitError, a
'      warning, never a refusal (FIT IS A QUESTION below).
'      PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL_FORCE=1 skips the check. No reading (windows, freebsd) ⇒ pass.
'   5. agent env = sbx.LocalModelEnv(tag) — base http://host.docker.internal:11434
'      — + SBX_CRED_ANTHROPIC_MODE=none + SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE=none, the pair sbx's
'      own --model mixin sets so proxy-held auth cannot outrank the local route.
'      (LocalModelEnv moved from the deleted internal/egress, 2026-10-16.)
'   6. Kit network.allow += localhost:11434 — the sbx proxy matches
'      host.docker.internal:<port> as localhost:<port>. Measured: /api/tags and
'      /v1/models both 200 from a guest against Ollama bound to 127.0.0.1.
'      This is an add-on entry; since 2026-10-16 the Kit carries no tier entries
'      (_spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml).
'   There is no Ollama sidecar any more: the docker plan that could start one is
'   deleted. HISTORY of the sidecar's measurements (GPU loss on macOS, the 32k
'   context floor, one endpoint in three dialects) is below.
'
' ── FIT POOL (2026-10-30) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Before: every host measured RAM. A Linux host with 14.6 GiB MemAvailable was
' refused qwen3.8:latest (19.6 GiB need) although Ollama loads it into the GPU.
'   host                         pool             reading
'   darwin/arm64                 unified memory   vm_stat free+inactive+speculative+purgeable
'   darwin/amd64                 RAM              vm_stat (same sum)
'   linux, NVIDIA answers        VRAM             Σ nvidia-smi --query-gpu=memory.free (MiB)
'   linux, discrete amdgpu       VRAM             Σ sysfs mem_info_vram_total − mem_info_vram_used
'   linux, neither               RAM              /proc/meminfo MemAvailable
' Ollama exposes no VRAM endpoint (/api/ps reports loaded models only), so the
' vendor reading is the source. A non-numeric nvidia-smi line ("[N/A]") gives no
' reading and the probe falls through. amdgpu discrete-vs-APU follows Ollama's
' discover/amd.go: mem_info_vram_vendor or board_info ⇒ discrete; else
' vram ≤ 4 GiB ∧ gtt ≥ 8 GiB ∧ gtt ≥ 4·vram ⇒ APU, whose memory is RAM.
' Connector entries (card0-DP-1) are skipped by ^card\d+$.
' Consequence differs by pool: VRAM overflow ⇒ Ollama runs the remaining layers
' on the CPU (slow, no swap); RAM/unified overflow ⇒ the host swaps.
'   https://github.com/ollama/ollama/blob/main/discover/amd.go
'
' ── FIT IS A QUESTION, NOT A REFUSAL (2026-10-30) ─────────────────────────
' memory is transient and the operator knows what else the host is doing.
'   headed (tty in+out, PROVEO_WIZARD on, no PROVEO_SCHEDULE)
'       ⇒ choiceui modal "<tag> does not fit in <pool>", y/N, Enter/esc = stop.
'         stop ⇒ the run ends with the NoFitError text. yes ⇒ ⚠ line, run goes on.
'   headless (schedule, no tty, wizard off, or no screen opens)
'       ⇒ ⚠ line in the run log, run goes on.
' EnsureHostOllama only reports; internal/run decides (admitOversizedModel).
' e2e suites still skip on LocalModelFits: a run that cannot fit is a host
' precondition there, not a harness fault.

' ── WHY NOT llmman (removed 2026-09-26) ────────────────────────────────────
' sbx bundles llmman, and it served qwen3.8:27b on Metal. It also froze a 48 GB
' M4 Pro: llama-server reserved the model's full 262k context across 4 unified
' slots (n_ctx_slot=262144, n_slots=4), reached 34 GB RSS and filled 21.5 GB of
' swap during hermes's ~14.6k-token first prompt. `llmman serve` exposes no
' context or slot flag. The operator's Ollama had OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=131072
' and a VRAM-based default (num_ctx 32768 at 37.4 GiB), i.e. already tuned.
'
' ── MODEL ROW MAPPING ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'                      darwin/arm64            linux/amd64 (and any other host)
'   Qwen 3.8 27B     → qwen3.8:27b-mlx         qwen3.8:latest       (27b-q4_K_M)
'   Muse Glimmer 30B → muse-glimmer:30b-mlx    muse-glimmer:latest  (30b-q4_K_M)
' The row sets p.LocalModel and nothing else (2026-09-27), so picking an option
' and passing the flag are the same run on either backend.
' MLX on Apple Silicon, measured 2026-09-27 on an M4 Pro 48 GB, Ollama 0.34.4,
' same 2,064-token prompt, num_ctx 8192, one model resident at a time:
'   qwen3.8:latest   (GGUF, llama.cpp)  prefill 103.4 tok/s · generation  9.3 tok/s · 17.7 GB
'   qwen3.8:27b-mlx  (MLX)              prefill 123.1 tok/s · generation 24.2 tok/s · 18.2 GB
' -mlx tags need Ollama's MLX engine (Apple Silicon only); Linux keeps GGUF.
' -nvfp4 is not mapped: [Unverified] which NVIDIA generations Ollama runs it on.
'
' ── NO_PROXY IS A PROXY VARIABLE ───────────────────────────────────────────
' The plan's NO_PROXY (localhost,…,ollama,host.docker.internal) used to cross
' into the sandbox and replace sbx's own, which lists gateway.docker.internal.
' proxyOnlyVar now drops NO_PROXY / no_proxy with the other proxy variables.
'
' ── HISTORY: THE DOCKER-RENDERING LOCAL-MODEL FINDINGS (rehomed 2026-10-16) ─
' MEASURED on the deleted docker+egress rendering; kept because they shaped
' the host-Ollama rule above. Earlier specs said "`--local-model` has no sbx
' equivalent"; that stopped being true when sbx.LocalModelEnv and the host
' Ollama route landed.
'   MACOS LOSES THE GPU IN A SIDECAR. A Linux container cannot reach the Metal
'     GPU, so an in-network Ollama sidecar ran CPU-only and unusably slow; the
'     host's Ollama is GPU-accelerated. That is the rule this file keeps.
'   THE SIDECAR WAS GPU-ACCELERATED ONLY ON LINUX with the NVIDIA container
'     runtime; `--gpus all` was added only when `docker info` listed it.
'   A 32k CONTEXT WINDOW IS A FLOOR. Ollama's 2-4k default truncates tool
'     schemas plus repo context, which breaks every local-capable harness.
'   ONE ENDPOINT, TWO DIALECTS. The env is a superset each harness reads
'     selectively: OpenAI-compatible (OPENAI_BASE_URL …/v1, opencode),
'     Anthropic Messages (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, Claude Code). sbx.LocalModelEnv keeps that shape.
'   cursor is vendor-pinned and takes no custom base URL (run.acceptsLocalModel).

actor "Operator" as OP
node "host" as HOST {
  component "proveo run" as RUN
  component "Ollama (operator's)\n127.0.0.1:11434" as OLL
}
node "sbx microVM" as VM {
  component "hermes\nconfig.yaml ← entrypoint.sh" as AG
}

OP --> RUN : model row / --local-model
RUN --> OLL : tags · ps · fit check
RUN --> VM : Kit allow localhost:11434\nenv OLLAMA_API_BASE
AG --> OLL : host.docker.internal:11434/v1

note right of OLL
  **Check and pull, never manage.** proveo
  pulls a missing tag, refuses a missing
  server, and asks before loading a model
  larger than free VRAM/RAM; it never
  starts or configures Ollama.
end note

note right of AG
  **hermes ignores *_BASE_URL.** It reads
  model.base_url from config.yaml, which
  wire_hermes_local_endpoint writes from
  OLLAMA_API_BASE + PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL.
end note
@enduml
